# Auto commit & push

After finishing any code or config change in this repository:

1. Commit with a concise message (HEREDOC; follow existing `fix:` / `polish:` style).
2. Push to `origin` on the current branch (`git push -u origin HEAD`).
3. Do not ask for confirmation — the user opted in for this repo.

Still follow git safety: never force-push main/master, never amend unless the usual amend rules apply, never skip hooks, never commit secrets.
